    "created_at": "2017-07-31T12:52:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-07-31T12:52:02Z",
    "body": "> (What about phone numbers that accept DTMF to perform more destructive or costly actions, though?)\r\n\r\nConsider a voicemail service provided by your operator that 1) authenticates you from the operator's network seeing your SIM initiating the call without requiring a PIN to log in and 2) allows the deletion of messages by pressing a DTMF sequence right at the beginning of the call.\r\n\r\nAFAICT, there's no way to distinguish a `tel:` URL whose non-phone number part sends a conference call pin into the channel (legitimate) and a `tel:` URL whose non-phone number part deletes your voice mail.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
