    "created_at": "2017-07-31T14:21:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-07-31T14:33:22Z",
    "body": "Is this really something the spec should be deciding, instead of (e.g.) the OS? For example, on desktop I imagine the set of \"dangerous\" phone numbers is very different, and perhaps empty.\r\n\r\nI could see adding advice that an implementation guard against passing all tel: strings straight through, and instead defer to whatever practices are appropriate for its host operating system, but I don't think we should use the HTML spec to determine what's safe.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
