    "created_at": "2017-07-31T14:31:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-07-31T14:31:44Z",
    "body": "My point isn't that browsers shouldn't have guards (although as can be seen from those bugs, it appears at least Chrome is relying on OS protections instead of having its own). But that any guards will be OS-specific, and thus should not be specified in HTML.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
