    "created_at": "2017-08-07T19:14:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-08-07T19:14:48Z",
    "body": "Firefox has a guard today and that's causing real-world interop problems.  I'm happy with whatever path fixes the interop issue.  I don't know who would own such code in chromium, but I'm sure that if html says something about this and Firefox matches, we'll be happy to have chromium match.  Alternately if we can convince Firefox that their guard is unnecessary and they should (like Chromium) leave it up to the OS to filter, then sure that is an even faster way to fix the interop issue :-)",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
