    "created_at": "2017-08-07T20:23:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-08-07T20:23:57Z",
    "body": "I'd feel more comfortable if we had sign off on such a guard from WebKit (iOS, maybe macOS handoff) and Edge (Skype integration). In particular it seems unlikely the same guard is necessary for all those situations, so while it sounds like it might be possible for Firefox and Chrome to agree on a conservative guard, I'd be afraid of other vendors not wanting to restrict themselves to that same subset, and thus in practice the spec not reflecting an actual interoperable restriction.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
