    "created_at": "2017-08-08T09:28:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-08-08T09:28:57Z",
    "body": "> Do you know of any Android devices still within their support lifetime that ship with a dialer that has this problem?\r\n\r\nI haven't surveyed the space. However, I note that \"within their support lifetime\" is a problematic qualifier when it comes to Android. Part of what Firefox and Chrome provide on top of the Android base on ship-and-abandon Android devices is updated software that deals with potentially-hostile input from the network. While ideally Android as shipped would get security updates for the sort of time span people use a given device for, in practice users need security on devices that are not \"within their support lifetime\", so delegating to the part of the stack that doesn't get updated isn't really sufficient for practical purposes. (Even Google-branded devices have a security support lifetime that's shorter than the usable life of the device not considering the security aspect. And then for some brands it ranges to basically no security support at all.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
