    "created_at": "2017-08-08T12:53:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-08-08T12:53:16Z",
    "body": ">  However, I note that \"within their support lifetime\" is a problematic qualifier when it comes to Android. \r\n\r\nYeah, that's a good point - our bar should be higher.  FWIW I love my Nexus 7 tablet and was sad to see my google.com access blocked from it yesterday due to it being >1 year beyond security updates :-(\r\n\r\nStill, I'm confused why this would be important for Firefox but apparently not for Chrome (which tends to take security quite seriously, generally above platform interop).  I lack the technical context in this area myself to help drive the debate unfortunately.",
